## The disjoint window is impossible (checker upgrade)

The primary reported: 0 of the 3 swept window candidates is both
admissible and barrier-disjoint. The checker proved this is not a
sweep fact but a THEOREM under REQ4 as declared (monotonicity over
arbitrary R contained in R'): for any x outside R, monotonicity into
R + x plus disjointness there forces x outside W(R); ranging x forces
W(R) inside R, and disjointness at R itself then forces W(R) empty —
failing REQ5. **No non-empty record-determined window can be disjoint
from the barrier at all** (verified constructively on 12/12
configurations in the box). Scope caveat, stated exactly: the theorem
uses REQ4's declared arbitrary-superset form; the primary's harness
only TESTS REQ4 on depth-truncation chains. The landed model's
barrier/window separation therefore requires either a window that is
NOT record-determined or a breach of the declared requirement set —
the identification premise is now load-bearing in both directions.

